01:22:03,180 --> 01:22:08,190
(all hum)

2079
01:22:08,190 --> 01:22:14,190
Doesn't do much but it
sure lights the place, huh?

2080
01:22:14,690 --> 01:22:18,200
These guys are little,
but they'll crawl ya.

2081
01:22:18,200 --> 01:22:21,700
They're getting board.

2082
01:22:21,700 --> 01:22:27,210
Wait, Otto
Preminger's getting away.

2083
01:22:27,200 --> 01:22:30,200
Timber!

2084
01:22:30,210 --> 01:22:34,210
(dramatic classical music)

2085
01:22:34,710 --> 01:22:36,220
Wait a minute, they're
fighting each other

2086
01:22:36,210 --> 01:22:37,210
all of a sudden.

2087
01:22:37,210 --> 01:22:38,210
I don't get this.

2088
01:22:38,720 --> 01:22:40,220
I think it's the
end of the movie.

2089
01:22:40,220 --> 01:22:44,220
Oh.

2090
01:22:44,220 --> 01:22:45,730
No, stop, you're killing me.

2091
01:22:45,720 --> 01:22:47,220
(laughs)

2092
01:22:47,220 --> 01:22:48,720
This is weird.

2093
01:22:48,730 --> 01:22:51,230
These progressive
dance clubs are getting

2094
01:22:51,230 --> 01:22:53,730
out of hand.

2095
01:22:53,730 --> 01:22:56,240
Gentlemen, gentlemen, ooh.

2096
01:22:56,230 --> 01:23:00,230
Ow!

2097
01:23:00,240 --> 01:23:04,740
I am so ashamed.

2098
01:23:04,740 --> 01:23:10,250
Oh, lost my head over that one.

2099
01:23:10,250 --> 01:23:13,250
Dog pile on me, yay.

2100
01:23:13,250 --> 01:23:16,260
Just got to run to the
biffy, be right back.

2101
01:23:16,250 --> 01:23:20,250
Not an android, just
walking, calmly walking.

2102
01:23:20,260 --> 01:23:22,760
I've been spending
all movie inside

2103
01:23:22,760 --> 01:23:24,260
and it's beautiful out here.

2104
01:23:24,260 --> 01:23:26,770
Damn, mom's here.

2105
01:23:26,760 --> 01:23:33,260
(humming "Axel F")

2106
01:23:33,270 --> 01:23:36,280
I'm Howard Kiel, no
relation to Richard Kiel.

2107
01:23:36,270 --> 01:23:41,770
(dramatic classical music)

2108
01:23:41,780 --> 01:23:48,790
Finally, we meet
in the living room.

2109
01:23:48,790 --> 01:23:50,790
Don't try it,
they're decorative.

2110
01:23:50,790 --> 01:23:52,290
Be your last.

2111
01:23:52,290 --> 01:23:54,290
Your threats do not alarm me.

2112
01:23:54,290 --> 01:23:54,790
Okay they do.

2113
01:23:54,790 --> 01:23:57,300
You forget, I know no fear.

2114
01:23:57,290 --> 01:23:59,790
Androids have no
emotions, Martin.

2115
01:23:59,800 --> 01:24:00,800
Look what happened.

2116
01:24:00,800 --> 01:24:02,300
Hey, wipe my feet.

2117
01:24:02,300 --> 01:24:05,310
Professor Dornheimer, I
was not correctly programmed.

2118
01:24:05,300 --> 01:24:07,800
No duplicate of mine
is going to say that.

2119
01:24:07,810 --> 01:24:09,810
I must see the master.

2120
01:24:09,810 --> 01:24:11,810
I am the master here.

2121
01:24:11,810 --> 01:24:12,810
Do as I command you.

2122
01:24:12,810 --> 01:24:14,310
Not as I do.

2123
01:24:14,310 --> 01:24:15,820
Destroy this human being.

2124
01:24:15,810 --> 01:24:18,810
(dramatic classical music)

2125
01:24:18,820 --> 01:24:20,320
That is my twin.

2126
01:24:20,320 --> 01:24:21,820
We are not humans.

2127
01:24:21,820 --> 01:24:23,320
He is our enemy.

2128
01:24:23,320 --> 01:24:24,820
Kill him.

2129
01:24:24,820 --> 01:24:27,330
I want this "you"
situation taken care of.

2130
01:24:27,320 --> 01:24:29,320
I command you.

2131
01:24:29,330 --> 01:24:31,830
I am your master.

2132
01:24:31,830 --> 01:24:33,330
No, Kolos is the master.

2133
01:24:33,330 --> 01:24:34,830
I obey no other.

2134
01:24:34,830 --> 01:24:36,840
You stupid mechanical...

2135
01:24:36,830 --> 01:24:38,830
No Dad, not the belt.

2136
01:24:38,840 --> 01:24:44,840
Ow, my GI Joe arm. Ow.

2137
01:24:44,840 --> 01:24:47,350
The gloves are off, they're
tied up against the boards.

2138
01:24:47,340 --> 01:24:51,340
Lou Nanne is running
in to break it up.

2139
01:24:51,350 --> 01:24:53,850
Yeah, yeah that's the
spot, right there, yeah.

2140
01:24:53,850 --> 01:24:57,860
Hit him in the head,
they've got Hummel heads.

2141
01:24:57,860 --> 01:25:00,360
Virginia Grim,
thank God we're saved.

2142
01:25:00,360 --> 01:25:06,870
Did we come at a bad time?

2143
01:25:06,860 --> 01:25:10,360
Darling.

2144
01:25:10,370 --> 01:25:13,370
They died as they lived,
in each others arms.

2145
01:25:13,370 --> 01:25:15,380
But for GI Joe and
his fighting force,

2146
01:25:15,370 --> 01:25:17,370
there would be another day.

2147
01:25:17,370 --> 01:25:18,870
Eww.

2148
01:25:18,880 --> 01:25:21,880
Oh no, he's going to take
her to the tower, isn't he?

2149
01:25:21,880 --> 01:25:30,890
Did we get everything here?

2150
01:25:30,890 --> 01:25:31,890
(mimics thud)

2151
01:25:31,890 --> 01:25:32,390
Ow.

2152
01:25:32,390 --> 01:25:35,900
Sorry about your
head, I think.

2153
01:25:35,890 --> 01:25:38,890
Exit, stage left.

2154
01:25:38,900 --> 01:25:40,400
Somebody want to say
something, it's kind

2155
01:25:40,400 --> 01:25:45,910
of dragging here.

2156
01:25:45,900 --> 01:25:51,400
Someone drop this?

2157
01:25:51,410 --> 01:25:53,410
The hell?

2158
01:25:53,410 --> 01:25:54,410
Mr. Martin.

2159
01:25:54,410 --> 01:25:55,420
Call me Steve.

2160
01:25:55,410 --> 01:25:58,410
I was sent here to prepare
you society for conquest

2161
01:25:58,420 --> 01:26:00,420
by the masters of the galaxy.

2162
01:26:00,420 --> 01:26:01,920
But it didn't really pan out.

2163
01:26:01,920 --> 01:26:02,920
I have failed in my mission.

2164
01:26:02,920 --> 01:26:04,420
Big time.

2165
01:26:04,420 --> 01:26:06,430
I have failed not
because I am weak.

2166
01:26:06,420 --> 01:26:08,920
But because you are stronger.

2167
01:26:08,930 --> 01:26:11,930
I will leave your planet now.

2168
01:26:11,930 --> 01:26:14,430
I must return to a world of cold

2169
01:26:14,430 --> 01:26:16,940
and unemotional galaxy beings.

2170
01:26:16,930 --> 01:26:18,430
Minnesota?

2171
01:26:18,440 --> 01:26:20,440
I will give them my report

2172
01:26:20,440 --> 01:26:21,940
and then I will be destroyed

2173
01:26:21,940 --> 01:26:23,440
But enough about me.

2174
01:26:23,940 --> 01:26:25,450
But it will not matter.
You see, Mr. Martin,

2175
01:26:25,440 --> 01:26:29,940
I know now that I,
too, am an android.

2176
01:26:29,950 --> 01:26:32,950
Well, I didn't think they
piled human stuff that high.

2177
01:26:32,950 --> 01:26:34,450
(somber classical music)

2178
01:26:34,950 --> 01:26:38,460
(hocks)

2179
01:26:38,460 --> 01:26:43,960
Ah!

2180
01:26:43,960 --> 01:26:47,970
Am I Liz Taylor yet?

2181
01:26:47,970 --> 01:26:51,470
(humming)

2182
01:26:51,470 --> 01:26:55,980
Ew, you snicker-snagged on me.

2183
01:26:55,970 --> 01:27:02,970
♪ Oh, sweet mystery of life,
at last I've found you.

2184
01:27:02,980 --> 01:27:05,990
Well, I am off to be destroyed.

2185
01:27:05,980 --> 01:27:08,980
Transport safely, Dick.

2186
01:27:08,990 --> 01:27:11,490
What was that all about?

2187
01:27:11,490 --> 01:27:12,990
Well, another
day, another dollar.

2188
01:27:12,990 --> 01:27:15,500
You can check out
anytime you like

2189
01:27:15,490 --> 01:27:17,990
but you can never leave.

2190
01:27:18,000 --> 01:27:21,500
Where'd I park that spaceship?

2191
01:27:21,500 --> 01:27:24,500
I was at the airport,
I was in a cab here,

2192
01:27:24,500 --> 01:27:28,010
that's all I saw.

2193
01:27:28,010 --> 01:27:29,510
I wonder if that tickles?

2194
01:27:29,510 --> 01:27:34,510
I bet it does.

2195
01:27:34,510 --> 01:27:37,020
Mork calling Olsen,
Mork calling Olsen.

2196
01:27:37,010 --> 01:27:42,510
Come in Olsen.

2197
01:27:42,520 --> 01:27:46,030
What a weird day.

2198
01:27:46,020 --> 01:27:48,020
Ah, ah, ah, ah,

2199
01:27:48,030 --> 01:27:50,030
Staying alive, staying alive.

2200
01:27:50,030 --> 01:27:52,030
Ah, ah...

2201
01:27:52,030 --> 01:27:54,530
Na noo, na noo.

2202
01:27:54,530 --> 01:27:55,030
(chuckles)

2203
01:27:55,530 --> 01:27:56,530
Finally, finally the end.

2204
01:27:56,530 --> 01:27:58,530
(all cheer)

2205
01:27:58,540 --> 01:28:04,540
Alright.

2206
01:28:04,540 --> 01:28:12,950
(doors creak and whir)

2207
01:28:12,950 --> 01:28:14,450
Well I think I liked
her best in the part

2208
01:28:14,450 --> 01:28:16,460
of blue shorty with
the matching tights.

2209
01:28:16,450 --> 01:28:17,950
Crow, you have
got your taste up--

2210
01:28:17,960 --> 01:28:19,460
Alright, enough,
enough you two.

2211
01:28:19,460 --> 01:28:21,460
You know, despite all
the really dumb things

2212
01:28:21,460 --> 01:28:22,460
in today's movie,

2213
01:28:22,460 --> 01:28:24,960
I thought it was really great
that Richard Kiel finally

2214
01:28:24,960 --> 01:28:26,970
came out in the
end and confessed

2215
01:28:26,960 --> 01:28:29,460
that he was indeed an android.

2216
01:28:29,470 --> 01:28:32,470
I mean, it's not like we
didn't know it all along

2217
01:28:32,470 --> 01:28:34,970
but just to have to the
moxie to come out and say,

2218
01:28:34,970 --> 01:28:38,480
"Hey, this is who I
am, and I'm proud."

2219
01:28:38,480 --> 01:28:39,980
It's pretty neat, really.

2220
01:28:39,980 --> 01:28:41,980
Yeah, well it was really
just a matter of time

2221
01:28:41,980 --> 01:28:43,980
before he had to come out.

2222
01:28:43,980 --> 01:28:47,490
Have you seen this week's
issue of Robot Nation?

2223
01:28:47,480 --> 01:28:50,480
Aha! You know I always had a
hunch about him.

2224
01:28:50,490 --> 01:28:52,990
Yup, look at that,
every one of them.

2225
01:28:52,990 --> 01:28:56,500
Tweaky, the girl from Small
Wonder, Robbie the Robot,

2226
01:28:56,490 --> 01:28:57,490
Al Gore.

2227
01:28:57,490 --> 01:28:59,990
You know, I hear that
having dinner with R2D2

2228
01:29:00,000 --> 01:29:01,000
is just like admitting it.

2229
01:29:01,000 --> 01:29:03,000
Admitting what?

2230
01:29:03,000 --> 01:29:06,010
Joel, Tom and I have
something to tell you.

2231
01:29:06,000 --> 01:29:08,000
You two got into my
sewing kit again?

2232
01:29:08,010 --> 01:29:12,010
Joel, Joel, Joel, I wish
things were still that simple.

2233
01:29:12,010 --> 01:29:15,010
But, well, this is something
I think we've all known

2234
01:29:15,010 --> 01:29:16,520
for a long time.

2235
01:29:16,510 --> 01:29:18,510
I know we've alluded to it.

2236
01:29:18,520 --> 01:29:22,520
A stilted joke here,
a fleeting doubt there,

2237
01:29:22,520 --> 01:29:25,530
and yet never have
we actually said,

2238
01:29:25,520 --> 01:29:33,020
"Joel, Tom and I..."

2239
01:29:33,030 --> 01:29:34,530
Oh for crying out in the beer,

2240
01:29:34,530 --> 01:29:37,040
Joel, Crow and I are robots

2241
01:29:37,030 --> 01:29:38,530
and we want the world to know.

2242
01:29:39,040 --> 01:29:40,040
Well, Tom I knew that.

2243
01:29:40,040 --> 01:29:42,040
Now, can we get on
with this letter?

2244
01:29:42,040 --> 01:29:45,040
Sure, but Joel, how
did you already know?

2245
01:29:45,040 --> 01:29:48,550
Tom, it's more than a
little obvious, alright?

2246
01:29:48,550 --> 01:29:49,550
It is?

2247
01:29:49,550 --> 01:29:51,050
Let's put this up
on still store there.

2248
01:29:51,050 --> 01:29:54,550
This one is from a Kevin Jones

2249
01:29:54,550 --> 01:29:57,560
and it's from
Ypsilanti, Michigan.

2250
01:29:57,550 --> 01:30:00,550
He says, "Dear Joel, I like
Mystery Science Theater,

2251
01:30:00,560 --> 01:30:03,560
I watch your show every
time I get a chance.

2252
01:30:03,560 --> 01:30:06,070
I was just watching your show,
it's the one about the ghost

2253
01:30:06,060 --> 01:30:10,060
who haunts Tom Stewart,
I just saw him die.

2254
01:30:10,070 --> 01:30:12,070
Well, I'll tell you a
little about myself,

2255
01:30:12,070 --> 01:30:15,070
I'm 11 years old, my
name is Kevin Jones,

2256
01:30:15,070 --> 01:30:16,580
so write back to me, okay?

2257
01:30:16,570 --> 01:30:18,570
Sincerely, Kevin Jones.

2258
01:30:18,580 --> 01:30:20,080
We certainly will, Kevin

2259
01:30:20,080 --> 01:30:21,580
and if you would
like to write to us,

2260
01:30:21,580 --> 01:30:24,580
send your letters to the
Mystery Science Theater 3000

2261
01:30:24,580 --> 01:30:27,090
information club,
post office box 5325

2262
01:30:27,580 --> 01:30:30,080
Hopkins, Minnesota 55343.

2263
01:30:30,090 --> 01:30:31,090
You tell him?

2264
01:30:31,090 --> 01:30:32,090
He knew.

2265
01:30:32,090 --> 01:30:33,590
What up, sirs?

2266
01:30:33,590 --> 01:30:35,090
(laughing)

2267
01:30:35,090 --> 01:30:38,100
William Conrad is
actually gonna be here.

2268
01:30:38,100 --> 01:30:40,600
Like Cannon is
going to show up here.

2269
01:30:40,600 --> 01:30:42,100
I'm sure.

2270
01:30:42,100 --> 01:30:43,600
(alarm blares)

2271
01:30:44,100 --> 01:30:46,110
Frank, it's the big one.

2272
01:30:46,100 --> 01:30:47,100
Literally.

2273
01:30:47,100 --> 01:30:48,100
After him.

2274
01:30:48,110 --> 01:30:51,110
Oh, come on, relax, chief.
He's not gonna get far.

2275
01:30:51,110 --> 01:30:54,110
How true, how true.

2276
01:30:54,110 --> 01:30:57,120
What say, in honor of the
occasion, I press the button

2277
01:30:57,110 --> 01:30:58,110
this week.

2278
01:30:58,120 --> 01:30:58,620
It would be an honor.

2279
01:30:58,620 --> 01:31:01,990
Thank you, Frank.

2280
01:31:01,990 --> 01:31:05,382
(slow instrumental version of
"Love Theme from MST3K")

